# 2026-09-15 — Google Ads attribution → checkout-intent contract.
# The paywall's `POST /billing/checkout-intent` request body is enriched
# with `gclid` / `gbraid` / `wbraid` / `clickTimestamp` whenever the
# user landed via a Google Ads click. The backend DTO
# (`src/billing/dto/checkout-intent.request.dto.ts`, separate repo) must
# whitelist these exact four fields, because NestJS runs
# `ValidationPipe({ whitelist: true, forbidNonWhitelisted: true })` in
# `src/main.ts`. Any drift between these two files = 100% checkout
# failure for paid-search users (~80% of paying traffic).
#
# The bug lived Sep 5 → Sep 14 (backend PR #19 / commit `a4873f8`
# fixed it). 9 days of lost conversions. Full evidence in
# CLAUDE.md → "Ads attribution → checkout-intent DTO contract"
# and `.claude/specs/2026-09-14-paywall-invalid-request.md` (if present).
#
# `billing.service.ts` — the enrichment (lines 64–102). If you remove
#   any of `gclid`/`gbraid`/`wbraid`/`clickTimestamp` from `enriched`,
#   Google Ads Offline Conversion Import breaks. If you re-add fields
#   NOT declared in the backend DTO, every paid-ad user 400s.
# `google-click-id.ts` — cookie storage keys are `pdfvault_gclid` etc.
#   Renaming them silently orphans in-flight cookies; users who landed
#   yesterday lose attribution.
# `google-ads-click-boot.tsx` — URL query-string → cookie writer. Must
#   run on every landing page (mounted in root layout). Removing it =
#   attribution goes to zero across every campaign.
lib/shared/api/services/billing.service.ts
lib/client/analytics/google-click-id.ts
components/shared/google-ads-click-boot.tsx
